<h1>Mood Radio 0.1</h1>
<p class="date">25 November 2026</p>
<p>The first build for testers. Thank you for trying it.</p>
<h2>What to try</h2>
<ul><li>Pick a station from the shelves, or drag the target on the mood pad and save your own.</li><li><strong>More Like This</strong> steers the station toward the song playing now.</li><li><strong>Why</strong> shows what a track was picked for.</li><li><strong>New Discoveries</strong>, first on the For You shelf, plays songs you probably have not heard. Any station's <strong>Discoveries</strong> fader does the same in part.</li></ul>
<h2>Before you start</h2>
<ul><li>Mood Radio needs macOS 27 and an Apple Music subscription.</li><li>Open the invite link you were sent. It fills in the shared tags service and offers the sound model.</li></ul>
<h2>Known limits</h2>
<ul><li>Shared tags lean to one listener's taste for now, so jazz is thin.</li><li>A song with an unknown genre or year stays out of genre-only and era stations.</li></ul>
<h2>Reporting a problem</h2>
<ul><li><strong>Settings › Data › Copy Diagnostics</strong>, then paste it into a message with the time it happened.</li></ul>
]]></description>
